    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-floor offensive profile, anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66). **Jackson Merrill** is our strongest play, benefiting from a high-upside matchup against Littell (xERA 4.63) and a favorable park factor, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a strong platoon advantage against Canning, projecting as a high-efficiency start for our middle infield depth. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** also provide elite stability, despite facing Painter (xERA 4.32), as their respective power-speed combinations remain the engine of this roster. **Sam Antonacci** earns his spot in the outfield with a 66.09 score, bolstered by his lead-off role which maximizes his ability to steal bags\u2014a critical component of our strategy given our emphasis on SB scarcity.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Liam Hicks**, who fell just short of our 40.0 floor with a 39.58 score. While **Liam Hicks** possesses a solid platoon edge against McLean, the combination of a daunting 3.03 xERA for the opposing starter and unfavorable park dynamics suppressed his ceiling enough to keep him on the bench. We remain cautious with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (56.40) and **Josh Jung** (58.59); while both are safely in the lineup, they face elite arms in Bradish and Wacha, respectively. We are continuing to monitor the health of our depth chart, including **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, and **Drake Baldwin**, who all remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us with limited room for error should weather or late-scratches impact the performance of **Brayan Rocchio** or **Miguel Vargas**.",
